{% include 'fragments/greeting.j2' %}
<br>
<br>
This email is to let you know that the Nectar Research Cloud Application
Catalog service will be retired on <b>{{ shutdown_date }}</b>. Your project
<b>{{ project.name }}</b> has instances that were deployed through the
Application Catalog service, and they are listed below.
<br>
<br>
<h2>What is changing</h2>
<br>
From <b>{{ freeze_date }}</b>, new applications can no longer be deployed
from the Application Catalog service. Your existing instances keep running, and
you can keep using them as normal until {{ shutdown_date }}.
<br>
<br>
On {{ shutdown_date }} the Application Catalog service will be switched off.
<b>Your instances will not be deleted</b> at that point, but you will no
longer be able to manage them through the Applications panel in the
Dashboard. You can still manage them as ordinary instances from the
Instances panel.
<br>
<br>
<h2>What you need to do</h2>
<br>
<ul>
  <li>
    If you no longer need these instances, please delete them, along with
    any volumes you do not need.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you want to keep working, you can either keep your existing instances,
    or launch new ones directly from the matching image. Our guide explains
    how, including how to set up a DNS name and an HTTPS certificate, which
    the Application Catalog service used to do for you:
    <a href="{{ docs_url }}">{{ docs_url }}</a>
  </li>
  <li>
    For lighter R or Python work, the ARDC Nectar Jupyter Notebook Service
    may suit you better and needs no instance at all:
    <a href="https://jupyterhub.rc.nectar.org.au/">jupyterhub.rc.nectar.org.au</a>
  </li>
  <li>
    Back up any data you want to keep before you delete or replace an
    instance.
  </li>
</ul>
{% if environments -%}
<br>
<h2>Your Application Catalog service deployments</h2>
<table style="border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse;">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">Environment</th>
      <th style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">Application</th>
      <th style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">Instance</th>
      <th style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">Status</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for env in environments -%}
    {% for inst in env.instances -%}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">{{ env.name }}</td>
      <td style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">{{ inst.app }}</td>
      <td style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">{{ inst.name }} ({{ inst.id }})</td>
      <td style="padding: 0.5em; border: 1px solid black; text-align: left;">{{ inst.status }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor -%}
    {% endfor -%}
  </tbody>
</table>
<br>
{% endif -%}
<br>
If you have any questions, or need help moving your work, please reply to
this email or contact <a href="mailto:support@ehelp.edu.au">support@ehelp.edu.au</a>.
<br>
<br>
Regards,
<br>
ARDC Nectar Research Cloud Support Team
<br>
<br>
<small><i>You are receiving this email because you are a member of a Nectar
Research Cloud project that has instances deployed through the Application
Catalog service.</i></small>
